# Intent: Faces core, part 2 (owner brief 2026-11-16). The saved face settings and what drives the face. Styles are now Big eyes (the default), Eyes only, Stock (the original skin as shipped), Classic (rounder eyes) and Minimal; round, cat, robot, sleepy, retro pixel and heart eyes are dropped as styles, and a saved or sent one loads as Big eyes (the blob is version 3, versions 1 and 2 are still read; the saved ids 3 to 8 are the dropped ones, the new ones are 9 and 10 so a saved dropped id can never turn into a new style). The colour rule: the eyes are white by default (colour still sets them), the screen colour behind the face is per person (a palette colour at 26 percent of its brightness, or a dark #rrggbb; a colour too bright for white eyes is refused), and the gentle emotion tint is a setting that is on by default. The sweat and shy decorators are dropped (their ids stay; the names are unknown) and the built-in reactions that used the sweat drop have none. The thinking cue is the skin's own dots (patch X01). The low-battery look is TIRED, not sad: half-lidded eyes, a slow blink and a yawn at 20 percent, more droop at 10 percent, the sleepy face at 5 percent, set from the battery ladder each poll and cleared by a cable; a well cared for unit rests content (round eyes, a small smile) instead of cutting its eyes with the happy lid. The display maps surprised, tired, love, content and closing, and sleeping now closes the lids over 1.5 s. Bench builds get self.face.bench_emotion.
# Placement: unit (settings are kept in the unit's own flash; the host copy is what the settings page shows)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/{maipai_face_core.h,maipai_face.cc,maipai_face.h,maipai_decor_core.h,maipai_decor.cc,maipai_react_core.h,maipai_daily.cc,maipai_facebench.cc} and board/stackchan_display.cc (ours, patches F01, U01, U02, U06, T01, M01, H01); maipai_pack_core.h of U06 is deleted: the styles are rows of maipai_look_core.h now
# Check after a flash: self.face.get_config shows style big_eyes, background none, emotion_tint true on a unit with no saved face; a saved classic stays classic; a battery simulation at 20, 10 and 5 percent shows the tired looks and a cable clears them.

